    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the shortcoming of tree-ring-based temperature reconstructions, which fail to show the significant short-term cooling predicted by climate models in the years immediately following major volcanic eruptions.",
    "method": "We propose a hypothesis, supported by a tree-growth model, that severe post-eruption cold causes missing tree rings, and the resulting dating errors in composite records cause the volcanic cooling signal to appear muted and smeared in large-scale reconstructions.",
    "task": "The task is to debate and explain the discrepancy whereby tree-ring-based temperature reconstructions show a muted cooling response to large volcanic eruptions, in contrast to the significant cooling predicted by climate models.",
